@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Spec conventions — roles, arrow intent, and the SPEC reference lifecycle

component "<<app>>  first-party app / runtime service" as R1 <<app>>
queue     "<<async>>  queue · scheduler · background" as R2 <<async>>
node      "<<host>>  host / platform / operator boundary" as R3 <<host>>
cloud     "<<cloud>>  external SaaS / vendor" as R4 <<cloud>>
database  "<<db>>  persistence / state store" as R5 <<db>>
component "<<error>>  destructive · failure · security-sensitive" as R6 <<error>>

R1 ARROW_MAIN     R2 : ARROW_MAIN — primary / synchronous
R2 ARROW_QUEUE    R3 : ARROW_QUEUE — internal async hand-off
R3 ARROW_OPTIONAL R5 : ARROW_OPTIONAL — alt · retry · optional
R3 ARROW_CLOUD    R4 : ARROW_CLOUD — crosses to an external system
R1 ARROW_ERROR    R6 : ARROW_ERROR — failure / destructive

note bottom of R6
  **No renders in the tree.** ""_spec/"" holds sources: ""\.puml"", ""\.mmd"",
  ""\.vega\.json"". A committed ""\.svg"" or ""\.png"" goes stale the moment its
  source changes, and nothing makes the staleness visible — so
  ""_spec/**/*\.svg"" and ""*\.png"" are gitignored, and ""plantuml -checkonly""
  (which writes no file) is the gate before committing. Render to a scratch
  path when you need to look at a picture.

  The one exception is ""_spec/_assets/"": curated documentation images the
  README embeds, produced by hand or by ""vhs"" from a ""\.tape"" — authored
  artifacts, not diagram output.
end note

note top of R1
  **Directory rule.** ""_spec/"" mirrors the source tree —
  ""_spec/internal/<pkg>/"", ""_spec/cmd/<bin>/"",
  ""_spec/defs/<name>/"", ""_spec/packages/lib/"". A folder
  that does **not** correspond to a live source folder is
  prefixed with an underscore: ""_assets"", ""_paradigms"",
  ""_conventions"", ""_experiments"", ""_refactors"",
  ""_devops"" (build · publish pipeline), ""_runtimes""
  (toolchains available inside a harness).
end note

note bottom of R3
  **Identity is remote.** Every diagram includes
  ""proveo.puml"" from the identity repo, so the palette
  changes in one place. Legacy files using the older
  includeurl form of ""proveo.iuml"" with the ""PATH_MAIN""
  and ""errorLabel"" macros still render — those names are
  kept as aliases — but author new work with stereotypes
  and the ""ARROW_*"" macros.
end note

note bottom of R5
  **Text.** A doubled-quote pair marks ""monospace"" — use
  it for identifiers, paths and env vars; **bold** for
  section labels; //italic// for concepts.

  Because that delimiter //is// a quote pair, a literal
  double quote inside a label miscounts it: write string
  literals with single quotes, as in 'pause'.
end note

note bottom of R6
  **SPEC lifecycle — what keeps diagrams honest:**
  * every ""\.puml"" is referenced from at least one source
    file, on one top-line ""SPEC:"" comment (comma-separated)
  * source deleted or renamed → move the comment to the
    file that replaced the behavior; do not delete the diagram
  * delete a diagram only when the whole feature is gone;
    reimplemented on new tech → mark it OUTDATED instead
  * refactor moves logic → move the comment, update the
    diagram if the architecture actually changed
  * ""_spec/_refactors/"" (frozen snapshots) and
    ""_spec/_plans/"" (designs with no code yet) are exempt
    from the referencing rule — nothing exists to link them
    from. A ""_plans"" diagram is titled PLANNED and moves
    out (or is deleted) once it ships.

  **Default to current-state truth.** Keep future
  direction in notes; never rename a current component to
  the abstraction it is meant to grow into.

  **Validate before committing:** ""plantuml -checkonly f.puml""
  (empty output + exit 0 = clean).
end note

